dibenzo-<italic>p</italic>-dioxins, polychlorinated dibenzofurans, and coplanar poly-chlorinated biphenyls in breast milk from two cities in Ukraine</article-title><source>J Toxicol Environ Health A</source><volume>58</volume><fpage>119</fpage><lpage>127</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10522644</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b8-ehp0116-000626"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Guo</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Hendrickx</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name><name><surname>Overstreet</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Dieter</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Stewart</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Tarantal</surname><given-names>AF</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Endocrine biomarkers of early fetal loss in cynomolgus macaques (<italic>Macaca fascicularis</italic>) following exposure to dioxin</article-title><source>Biol Reprod</source><volume>60</volume><fpage>707</fpage><lpage>713</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10026120</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-ehp0116-000626"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Guo</surname><given-names>YL</given-names></name><name><surname>Lambert</surname><given-names>GH</given-names></name><name><surname>Hsu</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name></person-group><year>1995</year><article-title>Growth abnormalities in the population exposed <italic>in utero</italic> and early postnatally to poly-chlorinated biphenyls and dibenzofurans</article-title><source>Environ Health Perspect</source><volume>103</volume><issue>suppl 6</issue><fpage>117</fpage><lpage>122</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8549457</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10-ehp0116-000626"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hayabuchi</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Yoshimura</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuratsune</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1979</year><article-title>Consumption of toxic rice oil by &#x02018;Yusho&#x02019; patients and its relation to the clinical response and latent period</article-title><source>Food Cosmet Toxicol</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>455</fpage><lpage>461</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">118100</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11-ehp0116-000626"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hirota</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Kataoka</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hirohata</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Kuratsune</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Yoshimura</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Hori</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Okumura</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Masuda</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Annual health examination of Yusho patients</article-title><source>Yusho: A Human Disaster Caused by PCBs and Related Compounds</source><publisher-loc>Fukuoka, Japan</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Kyushu University Press</publisher-name><fpage>249</fpage><lpage>266</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b12-ehp0116-000626"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Iida</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Todaka</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Measurement of dioxins in human blood: improvement of analytical method</article-title><source>Ind Health</source><volume>41</volume><fpage>197</fpage><lpage>204</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12916750</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13-ehp0116-000626"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ikeda</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Comparison of clinical picture between Yusho/Yucheng cases and occupational PCB poisoning cases</article-title><source>Chemosphere</source><volume>32</volume><fpage>559</fpage><lpage>566</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8907233</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b14-ehp0116-000626"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kunita</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Hori</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Obana</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Otake</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Nishimura</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kashimoto</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1985</year><article-title>Biological effect of PCBs, PCQs and PCDFs present in the oil causing yusho and yucheng</article-title><source>Environ Health Perspect</source><volume>59</volume><fpage>79</fpage><lpage>84</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3921369</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b15-ehp0116-000626"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kusuda</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1971</year><article-title>Yusho and female:studies on sexual functions in female patients with rice oil poisoning [In Japanese]</article-title><source>Sanka to Fujinka</source><volume>38</volume><fpage>1063</fpage><lpage>1072</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b16-ehp0116-000626"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Masuda</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Fate of PCDF