ic>n</italic> = 15)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">PeCDF</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">7.25 (2.2&#x02013;26.0)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2,899.3 (112.1&#x02013;19942.7)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">697.7 (52.4&#x02013;2289.6)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">39.5 (4.0&#x02013;951.8)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">PCB-126</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">41.6 (5.0&#x02013;430.0)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">336.4 (89.5&#x02013;1705.3)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">159.0 (94.7&#x02013;330.5)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">60.4 (16.9&#x02013;118.8)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">PCB-169</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">37.1 (5.0&#x02013;160.0)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">759.6 (67.6&#x02013;4224.2)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">386.2 (61.5&#x02013;1041.5)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">70.6 (11.8&#x02013;499.1)</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn6-ehp0116-000626"><p>Geometric mean (minimum&#x02013;maximum). Data for the general population are from <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b17-ehp0116-000626">Masuda (2005)</xref>.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t5-ehp0116-000626" position="float"><label>Table 5</label><caption><p>Association of pregnancy outcomes with the estimated concentrations of PeCDF and PCBs 126 and 169.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Pregnancy outcome</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">PeCDF [OR (95% CI)<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn7-ehp0116-000626">a</xref><italic>p</italic>-value<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn8-ehp0116-000626">b</xref>]</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">PCB-126 [OR (95% CI)<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn7-ehp0116-000626">a</xref><italic>p</italic>-value<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn8-ehp0116-000626">b</xref>]</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">PCB-169 [OR (95% CI)<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn7-ehp0116-000626">a</xref><italic>p</italic>-value<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn8-ehp0116-000626">b</xref>]</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Induced abortion among all pregnancies</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.82 (1.21&#x02013;2.74) &#x0003c; 0.01</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4.14 (1.30&#x02013;13.19) 0.02</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3.47 (1.58&#x02013;7.61) &#x0003c; 0.01</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Spontaneous abortion among pregnancies except induced abortions</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.60 (1.10&#x02013;2.33) 0.01</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.52 (0.92&#x02013;6.87) 0.07</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.28 (1.09&#x02013;4.75) 0.03</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Preterm delivery among all deliveries</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.98 (1.03&#x02013;3.80) 0.04</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4.90 (0.93&#x02013;25.75) 0.06</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4.12 (1.19&#x02013;14.30) 0.03</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Pregnancy loss among pregnancies except induced abortions<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn9-ehp0116-000626">c</xref></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.70 (1.18&#x02013;2.46) &#x0003c; 0.01</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.99 (1.16&#x02013;7.73) 0.02</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.68 (1.32&#x02013;5.48) &#x0003c; 0.01</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn7-ehp0116-000626"><label>a</label><p>OR for 10-fold increase in blood lipid level (95% CI) adjusted for age at delivery as a continuous variable, and the square of the age at delivery considering the possible curvature o